; A GENERIC INSTANTIATION used as a member/element type (`[pair<uint, tstr>]`) panics parsing at the
; group-entry catch-all (`not yet implemented: If you run into this please create a github issue`,
; parsing.rs). The same instantiation as a top-level rule RHS (`x = pair<uint, tstr>`,
; genericarg.multiple) is supported — the gap is the MEMBER position only. The matrix has no
; (member-role x genericarg) containment cells (role.generic-arg models the reverse: types AS
; generic args), so this hand fixture is the pin. Surfaced by the recombination sweep
; (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
pair<k, v> = [k, v]
a = [pair<uint, tstr>]
